<div class="container-fluid">
    <div class="card-box">
        <div class="col-md-12" style="padding:60px;">
            <h2>Our Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>Effective Date:</strong> August 26, 2025<br />
                <strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 8, 2026
            </p>

            <p>
                Welcome to Apparcus! We are operated by Apparcus Finexus Ltd, a technology service
                provider. We value your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal and
                financial information.
            </p>
            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and disclose your data when
                you use our platform (apparcus.com) and our mobile applications. By accessing or
                using our services, you agree to the terms described in this policy.
            </p>

            <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p>To provide The Organized Group Ledger and maintain our security standards, we collect:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Identity Information:</strong> Full Name, Date of Birth, Gender, and Photograph.</li>
                <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Phone Number and Email Address.</li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Personal Data:</strong> In compliance with CBN regulations, we collect your
                    Bank Verification Number (BVN) and National Identification Number (NIN) for identity
                    verification. Note: we do not store your BVN; it is encrypted and passed to our
                    licensed verification partners.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Financial Data:</strong> Virtual account numbers, transaction history, group
                    contribution records, and Beads balances.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Usage &amp; Technical Data:</strong> IP address, device type, operating system,
                    and access timestamps.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>2. Lawful Basis for Processing</h3>
            <p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act (NDPA) 2023, we process your data based on:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Consent:</strong> Your explicit permission given during sign-up.</li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Contract:</strong> To fulfill our obligation to manage your group records and
                    facilitate payments.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Legal Obligation:</strong> To comply with Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and Know
                    Your Customer (KYC) laws mandated by the CBN and EFCC.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
            <p>We use your data to:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Create and manage your Permanent Sub-accounts and transaction-based Virtual Accounts.</li>
                <li>Automate the Organized Group Ledger and provide real-time payment confirmation.</li>
                <li>Process Beads rewards and facilitate withdrawals to your personal bank account.</li>
                <li>Verify your identity via the NIBSS iGree protocol or Biometric Face Match.</li>
                <li>Detect and prevent fraud, money laundering, and unauthorized access.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>4. Sharing Your Information</h3>
            <p>
                We do not sell or rent your data. We only share information with trusted partners
                necessary for our operations:
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <strong>Banking Partner:</strong> Safe Haven Microfinance Bank (Safe Haven MFB), our
                    licensed custodian, for account creation and fund transfers.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Law Enforcement:</strong> When required by a valid legal request under Clause
                    5.12 of our Service Level Agreement or Nigerian law.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>5. Legal Compliance</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <strong>Nigeria:</strong> This policy is primarily governed by the Nigeria Data
                    Protection Act (NDPA) 2023.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>International:</strong> We also align with the principles of the General Data
                    Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) for users
                    accessing our services from other jurisdictions.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>6. Data Retention</h3>
            <p>
                In accordance with the Anti-Money Laundering (Prevention and Prohibition) Act 2022, we
                are legally required to retain your identity evidence and transaction records for a
                minimum of five (5) years after your account is closed or the business relationship
                ends. After this period, data is securely deleted or anonymized.
            </p>

            <h3>7. Compliance &amp; Anti-Money Laundering</h3>
            <p>
                Apparcus Finexus Ltd is committed to maintaining the highest standards of financial
                integrity. We operate a zero-tolerance policy toward money laundering, terrorism
                financing, and any form of financial crime.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Our Compliance Framework:</strong></p>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <strong>Identity Verification:</strong> In partnership with licensed institutions and
                    using NIBSS-approved protocols, we verify the identity of every Group Head and
                    contributor to ensure a secure ecosystem.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Transaction Monitoring:</strong> Our system utilizes automated logic to detect
                    and flag suspicious patterns, ensuring that communal funds are never used for illicit
                    activities.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Regulatory Reporting:</strong> We work closely with our banking partner, Safe
                    Haven MFB, and comply with all reporting requirements set by the Central Bank of
                    Nigeria (CBN) and the Nigerian Financial Intelligence Unit (NFIU).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Prohibited Uses:</strong> Apparcus strictly prohibits the use of its platform
                    for cryptocurrency trading, unlicensed FX transactions, or any fraudulent
                    get-rich-quick schemes.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>8. Your Rights and Choices</h3>
            <p>As an Apparcus user, you have the right to:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
                <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> Correct any inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Withdrawal of Consent:</strong> You may withdraw your consent for data
                    processing (this may limit your access to financial features).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your data, subject to the 5-year
                    mandatory retention rule for financial records.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>9. Security of Your Data</h3>
            <p>
                We implement high level security protocols, including End-to-End Encryption (AES-256),
                secure firewalls, and multi-factor authentication (MFA) for withdrawals. While we strive
                for absolute protection, no system is 100% impenetrable; we encourage you to keep your
                Apparcus PIN and Login Password confidential.
            </p>

            <h3>10. Cookies and Tracking</h3>
            <p>
                We use cookies to remember your preferences and analyze how you interact with the
                platform. You can manage cookie settings in your browser, but disabling them may affect
                app performance.
            </p>

            <h3>11. Age Restriction</h3>
            <p>
                Our services are intended for individuals aged 18 and above. We do not knowingly collect
                information from minors.
            </p>

            <h3>12. Third Party Links</h3>
            <p>
                Our website may contain links to external websites or services not controlled by
                Apparcus Finexus Ltd. We are not responsible for any third-party sites. We encourage you
                to review the policy of any external services you visit.
            </p>

            <h3>13. Changes to This Policy</h3>
            <p>
                We may update this policy to reflect regulatory changes. Significant updates will be
                communicated via email or an in-app notification.
            </p>

            <h3>14. Contact Us</h3>
            <p>
                If you have questions regarding your data or wish to exercise your rights, please
                contact us:
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Apparcus Finexus Ltd</strong><br />
